  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>917</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi></math>&nbsp; be the lowest wavelength of Lyman series then the lowest wavelength of Balmer series will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3668",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Using Rydberg&#39;s formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For the lowest wavelength in Lyman series,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>&#8734;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>For Balmer series,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>&#8734;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>917</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3668</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mover></math></p></blockquote>",
